  "id": "implementation-evaluation",
  "term": "implementation evaluation",
  "definition": "Implementation evaluation is the assessment of how an intervention or program is put into practice and whether its planned activities are being carried out in ways that extend reach, encourage uptake, and show early effectiveness. It focuses on implementation outcomes such as who the program reaches, how well it is adopted, and what results appear during delivery.",
